{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/285231-failing-to-recover-a-relic","id":285231,"title":"Failing to recover a relic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-17T13:13:30-07:00","id":285231,"title":"Failing to recover a relic","content":"If somebody steals a relic from a mummy tomb, the mummy can come after them, right? But what if the mummy fails to recover the relic. Do they get another chance, or do they only 'spawn' once to deal with this sort of thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T13:54:53-07:00","id":285304,"title":"","content":"If your remains are disturbed the Call is automatic, pouring Sekhem into your frame to incarnate an avatar of righteous vengeance. I believe this is also the case when a stranger violates your tomb by removing anything from within it. In such a case, the likelihood of them getting away with it is pretty small.<br /> <br /> When I say stranger, I mean someone not of your cult who would otherwise not have rightful access to your tomb. And this is important, because your high priest in your cult could go off the reservation and remove something from the tomb and it might not trigger your awakening. Or such is my inference, in part from the chapter fiction, and I know that is a dangerous inference to make. Nevertheless it's true that cult members must probably move your Relics and undertake a ritual around them to normally awaken you, so it stands to reason that people usually allowed to be there and touch things will not awaken you in a murderous rage by being there and touching things.<br /> <br /> But, okay. Say something from your tomb is stolen by a treasure hunter. You could spend a Descent trying to get the item back and take your vengeance; your Sekhem could burn out before you're successful. Your return to henet, but your cult can always call you back to continue your quest for vengeance. In that case though, &quot;recover my lost relic&quot; is a purpose given by your cult upon awakening, not by the nature of the Rite of Return that demands you seek punishment for tomb violation.<br /> <br /> However in such a case there's not a practical distinction in the effect.<br /> <br /> Now, take another situation. Your tomb is plundered by the minions of another Mummy. You arise due to the violation, pursue them, etc. By the time you catch up with them, that other Mummy has returned to henet and taken the relic into Duat with them. Arguably you can't fulfill your purpose that well aside from slaughtering your enemy's cult (since plundering another's tomb is generally frowned on, but they did it to you); however the Relic is <i>gone</i>. So you can't get it back; may as well make the thieves pay (which you're still sorcerously bound to do anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T01:27:48-07:00","id":285774,"title":"","content":"The other thing to note is that Mummies have a magic sense called Kepher that enables them to sense relics. It's at its strongest when dealing with relics they once kept in their own tombs. No matter where in the world the relic is, the Mummy can track it down by rolling their Sekhem-2.<br /> <br /> At Memory 3, the default, a Mummy remembers a decent chunk of their most recent Descent as well. Something as notable as &quot;someone stole a relic from me&quot; almost certainly means that they'll remember the relic going missing, and know to try and locate it with Kepher.<br /> <br /> Everything Zelbinnean said holds true as well. In effect, if a Mummy fails to retrieve their relic in a single descent, and it hasn't been sent to Duat, they still stand a very good chance of locating it the next time they're woken. They will need to wait until their cult finds some way to perform the Call, however, unless a Sothic Turn is imminent or someone disturbs their remains in the meantime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T06:27:24-07:00","id":285839,"title":"","content":"I was re-reading the Kepher rules and rolling some white room dice, and I realized how much they suck at finding any relic that isn't their's, especially/mostly once they're down to Sekhem 6 or less","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T07:02:16-07:00","id":285859,"title":"","content":"The ability to spend Willpower helps a lot, but yeah... we've noticed that. During the first session though, Kepher is fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T07:37:53-07:00","id":285907,"title":"","content":"Yeah lol I remember reading how your planned four sessions were condensed into one because of the unforeseen awesomeness of Kepher. But even trying to find a relic that isn't your's but that you've at least <i>seen</i> or <i>held</i> nets you a -4 penalty, and at Sekhem 5 without Willpower you're rolling a chance die","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T08:55:29-07:00","id":285954,"title":"","content":"I think there are a couple general Guild Affinities with bonuses that help with kepher rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}